// Test: kernel must be host-runtime-free — a kernel that uses host runtime is rejected.
// Device modules cannot reference String/heap/registry machinery; `--kernel` must
// fail with a clear diagnostic instead of emitting broken NVPTX code.
// @test: kernel rejects host-runtime symbols
// @description: --kernel rejects modules that pull in __vyb_* host runtime (issue #198)
// @category: kernel
// @expect: fail
// @expect-error: Kernel module references host-runtime symbols
// @vyb-args: --kernel

// A String value forces the host string registry into the module, which is
// forbidden on the GPU. Without core::auto-import a bare String type still
// resolves, and using one emits __vyb_string_retain/__vyb_string_free.
make_greeting(name<String>)<String> -> {
    return name
}
